- After: `\"The parent-first rule uses one shared approval predicate with approval-act readers...\"`\n  - Why: states the shared, case-insensitive approval predicate and its absent/out-of-vocabulary behavior.\n\n- LLR-358 `detail`\n  - Before: `\"The commit judgement compares the first listed carrier for every changed spine tier...\"`\n  - After: `\"Once any spine carrier changes, the commit judgement reads all four spine tiers ... from ... TOML and legacy forms...\"`\n  - Why: corrects all-tier reading, carrier precedence, side-specific absence, single staged merge parent, and pre-commit-step behavior.\n\n- TC-396 `method`\n  - Before: `\"Exercise the in-process parent-first rule...\"`\n  - After: `\"Exercise the shared, case-insensitive Approved-or-Founded predicate and the in-process parent-first rule...\"`\n  - Why: states the `test_the_approval_pair_has_one_home` arm.\n\n- TC-396 `expected`\n  - Before: `\"Each Approved or Founded child under a declared parent...\"`\n  - After: `\"The shared predicate recognizes Approved or Founded regardless of letter case and rejects an absent or out-of-vocabulary status...\"`\n  - Why: matches LLR-357’s shared-predicate contract.\n\n- TC-397 `method`\n  - Before: `\"every merge parent ... the legacy carrier; ... hook, and trunk-freshness exclusion.\"`\n  - After: `\"the merge parent ... first listed carrier among TOML and legacy forms; ... pre-commit hook.\"`\n  - Why: removes the unstated trunk-freshness claim and matches actual merge/carrier behavior.\n\n- TC-397 `expected`\n  - Before: `\"an untouched or absent spine registry ... comparison-side failures...\"`\n  - After: distinguishes absent current-side/no-refusal from absent comparison-side/all-statuses-moved and added-inconsistent-registry refusal.\n  - Why: makes the missing-registry arms testable and unambiguous.\n\nChecks:\n\n- `trace.py --strict` — passed: `orphans=0 integrity=0`.\n- `check_trajectory.py --strict` — launched, but its repository scan remained activ